B = [
('Braun', 'Europe', '1950s-70s', 'electronics', 'In the style of Braun, calm functional German industrial design of the 1950s to 1970s. Plain rectangular boxes with softly radiused corners, matte satin-finish sheet metal or textured plastic in off-white, pale grey, black and graphite. Controls are small round dials, short slide switches and flush push buttons, grouped in neat grids and set in a ruled layout. Tiny accents of orange, yellow or green mark the key control. Lettering is lowercase or clean grotesque sans-serif, thin and evenly spaced, printed in black or white on the face. Speaker grilles are fine perforated or slotted aluminium. Shavers, clocks, radios, record players and kitchen blenders share this quiet, honest, ornament-free look with generous empty space and precise tolerances.'),
('Apple', 'North America', '2000s-present', 'electronics', 'In the style of Apple, minimalist consumer electronics with seamless slab forms. Thin rectangles with uniformly rounded corners and continuous tight radii, milled aluminium bodies in silver, space grey, gold and soft pastel anodised colours, edge-to-edge glass fronts with thin black bezels. Glossy white polycarbonate in the early 2000s, then brushed metal unibody construction. No visible screws, almost no buttons, only a few precisely cut slim keys, circular camera lenses grouped on a glass back, and a small polished logo silhouette of a bitten fruit centred on the rear. Interfaces use clean sans-serif type, generous white space, soft translucent blur layers and glossy rounded icons. Packaging is white and sparse. Mood is clean, premium and calm.'),
('Sony', 'East Asia', '1980s-90s', 'electronics', 'In the style of Sony, Japanese consumer electronics of the 1980s and 1990s. Compact black or silver boxes with beveled edges, brushed aluminium faceplates and dense rows of small rectangular rubber or plastic buttons. Portable cassette players in metallic blue and silver with orange accents, Trinitron televisions with deep black cabinets and flat-sided tubes, mini hi-fi stacks with tiny green and amber LED level meters and blue-green vacuum fluorescent displays. Fine stencil-like capital sans-serif labels, thin embossed model numbers, small rounded corners and engineered, high-tech miniaturised proportions. Later years bring minimalist matte black slabs with glowing coloured lighting strips. Mood is precise, technical and aspirational.'),
('Technics', 'East Asia', '1970s-80s', 'electronics', 'In the style of Technics, 1970s and 1980s Japanese hi-fi separates. Wide flat black or silver components with thick brushed aluminium front panels, heavy rotary knobs with knurled edges, rows of slim piano-style push keys, and rectangular illuminated meters with needle gauges or segmented green and amber LEDs. Direct-drive turntables with a flat rectangular plinth in black or silver, a strobe-dotted platter ring, a slim tonearm and a large pitch slider with finger-sized fader. Neat fine white sans-serif lettering, small engraved scale lines, rack-mount proportions and glossy dark smoked acrylic lids. Mood is serious, studio-grade and quietly luxurious.'),
('Nintendo', 'East Asia', '1980s-present', 'toys', 'In the style of Nintendo, playful Japanese game hardware. Compact rounded rectangles with chunky friendly proportions, glossy and matte plastic in white, light grey, red, black and bright primary or pastel colours. Controllers have a cross-shaped directional pad, small round coloured face buttons in red, blue, yellow or green, and short slim start keys, all set in tidy symmetrical layouts. The 1980s look has a cream-grey case with dark red trim and gold-lettered labels, boxy cartridges with ridged grips and rectangular stickers. Later devices use clean white or black slab shells, thin colourful detachable controllers, and rounded sans-serif logo lettering in red. Mood is cheerful, approachable and toy-like but neatly built.'),
('Sega', 'East Asia', '1990s', 'electronics', 'In the style of Sega, 1990s Japanese game consoles and arcade hardware. Glossy black plastic shells with sharp angular wedge shapes and circular recessed cartridge slots, moulded ridges and vents, curved controller grips with three or six oversized round buttons and a round directional disc. Cobalt blue lettering and swirl logos, white and orange accents, loud saturated cabinet artwork with bold outlines and hard-edged speed lines, and glowing red or green power LEDs. Dreamcast-era units are pale off-white and square with a soft spiral on the lid. Typography is slanted bold italic capitals with a futuristic, fast feel. Mood is edgy, energetic and arcade-bright.'),
('Atari', 'North America', '1970s-80s', 'electronics', 'In the style of Atari, late 1970s and early 1980s American home game consoles and computers. Heavy wedge-shaped boxes clad in simulated dark woodgrain vinyl on the front with black ribbed plastic tops, chunky silver toggle switches in a row along the top edge, and thick black joysticks with a single round red button on a square base. Warm brown, black and silver palette. Cartridges are black with ridged grips and brightly illustrated paper labels showing painted spacescapes in orange, purple and teal. Logo is a stylised three-bar fuji-like trident shape in white or red with rounded geometric capitals. Computers are beige-grey with chunky keys. Mood is warm, retro-futuristic, 1970s den.'),
('Commodore', 'North America', '1980s', 'electronics', 'In the style of Commodore, 1980s home computers. Wide beige or brown-beige plastic keyboard-case computers with a sloped wedge profile, thick rows of chunky rectangular keys with grey and light-brown caps carrying coloured graphic symbols on their fronts, a rainbow-coloured stripe or slim dark band across the case, tiny red power LEDs and a ribbed vent grille. Matching cream-coloured floppy disk drives and cassette decks, joysticks with black bases and red fire buttons, and boxy CRT monitors with rounded dark bezels. Interfaces show a blue screen with a light-blue border and blocky pixel text. Logo is a bold angular chevron mark in stylised capitals. Mood is nerdy, hobbyist and cosy.'),
('Olivetti', 'Europe', '1950s-70s', 'electronics', 'In the style of Olivetti, Italian office machines of the 1950s to 1970s treated as sculpture. Typewriters in bright signal red, lemon yellow, teal and orange glossy moulded plastic or pressed steel with soft flowing organic curves, rounded keyboards with white round-topped keys, and compact carry-case shells in matching colours. Calculators and computer cabinets have smooth enamelled panels, recessed rows of tiny coloured keys and small round dials. Lettering is lower-case or rounded sans-serif in white or black, often a small stripe of colour on the face. Mood is playful, elegant, optimistic and artisanal, with simple shapes polished to a gleaming industrial finish.'),
('Bang & Olufsen', 'Europe', '1960s-present', 'electronics', 'In the style of Bang & Olufsen, Danish luxury audio and television design. Slender, tall, minimalist forms in brushed and polished aluminium, black glass and pale oiled wood, with thin plates floating in space, tapered pyramid or cone speakers, and fabric-covered grilles in charcoal or warm grey. Controls are almost invisible, with hairline touch strips, a single large circular dial, a slim slide-down panel hiding hidden buttons, and subtle white or amber displays. Edges are razor-sharp with tiny perfectly even gaps. Palette is silver, black, natural oak, dark walnut and occasional soft earthy tones. Lettering is tiny, thin and lowercase. Mood is refined, sculptural and serene.'),
('Leica', 'Europe', '1930s-present', 'cameras', 'In the style of Leica, German rangefinder cameras. Compact rectangular bodies with a flat top plate, black enamel paint or polished silver chrome, wrapped in finely pebbled black vulcanite leatherette. A small viewfinder window and coupled range window sit at the top front, with a knurled shutter-speed dial, a thin film-advance lever and a round rewind knob on top. Lenses are slim black or chrome barrels with fine knurled focusing rings, engraved white and red distance and aperture numerals, and a small red dot on the front. Minimal, no clutter, brass showing through worn paint on edges. Lettering is a small script logo in white. Mood is understated, crafted and timeless.'),
('Hasselblad', 'Europe', '1950s-present', 'cameras', 'In the style of Hasselblad, Swedish medium-format cameras. A cubic body with a square profile, finished in satin black paint with bright chrome trim or all-black crinkle texture, topped with a folding waist-level viewfinder hood or a pentaprism. A large detachable square film magazine fits the back and a big round lens with chrome or black barrel, coloured aperture and shutter rings, and engraved white numerals mounts at the front. Winding crank on the side, a single large shutter button, and a bold white capital wordmark. Special editions use bright colours or exposed carbon. Mood is serious, rugged, professional and sculptural.'),
('Polaroid', 'North America', '1970s-80s', 'cameras', 'In the style of Polaroid, instant film cameras of the 1970s and 1980s. Bulky, sleek folding or boxy bodies in beige, white or black plastic with a dark leatherette grip panel, a large single lens set above a bright rectangular flash bar and a big red rectangular shutter button. A chocolate-brown and tan palette is typical, with a rainbow stripe in red, orange, yellow, green and blue across the front. Film prints are square with a thick white border and a wide chin at the bottom, glossy surface, soft warm washed-out colours and slightly faded saturation. Lettering is bold rounded sans-serif in white. Mood is nostalgic, friendly and snapshot-casual.'),
('Nikon', 'East Asia', '1960s-80s', 'cameras', 'In the style of Nikon, Japanese single-lens reflex cameras of the 1960s to 1980s. Rugged, boxy bodies with a pentaprism hump, black enamel or silver chrome finish, and a leatherette covering with fine pebble grain. Heavy metal knurled dials on top for shutter speed and film rewind, a chunky film advance lever, and a bold yellow and black stripe on the lens mount. Lenses are black barrels with deep rubber-ribbed focus rings and engraved white, orange and green numerals. Wordmark is bold white capital letters on the prism front. Mood is rugged, professional and mechanical.'),
('Canon', 'East Asia', '1970s-80s', 'cameras', 'In the style of Canon, 1970s and 1980s Japanese film cameras. Compact boxy SLR bodies with a black or silver top plate, wood-grain or fine black leatherette covering, rows of tiny metal dials and small silver buttons, and a red-lettered diagonal bar logo. Lens barrels are black with subtle knurling and a red ring accent around the front of professional lenses. Bodies have a clean rectangular layout with a large angular pentaprism, a round film-speed dial and a thick advance lever. Lettering is a stylised red script mark. Mood is dependable, practical and quietly handsome.'),
('Fujifilm', 'East Asia', '2010s-present', 'cameras', 'In the style of Fujifilm, retro-styled digital cameras. Compact rangefinder-style bodies with a flat top plate in silver and black, finished in matte black paint over metal with a fine textured grip. Many machined aluminium dials sit on the top plate, each with engraved numerals for shutter speed, exposure compensation and film simulation, and a ring of chunky aperture rings around the lens barrel. A small offset viewfinder in the corner, red ruler-like labels, and a neat pebbled leatherette in black. Lettering is crisp white capitals. Mood is tactile, classic, clean and understated.'),
('Casio', 'East Asia', '1980s-present', 'watches', 'In the style of Casio, Japanese digital watches and calculators. Lightweight resin cases in black, grey, silver or bright primary colours with squared-off octagonal or rectangular bezels, grey-green LCD displays showing chunky segmented digits, and small rubber push buttons on the sides labelled in tiny white capitals. Resin straps with moulded loops, steel bracelet versions with a gold finish, and tough rubberised protective bezels in G-shock style. Calculators have grid layouts of coloured keys in grey, orange and blue. Printed text is dense, small and technical, with many function labels around the dial. Mood is cheap, functional, geeky and indestructible.'),
('Seiko', 'East Asia', '1960s-80s', 'watches', 'In the style of Seiko, Japanese wristwatches of the 1960s to 1980s. Stainless steel cases with sharp faceted lugs, polished and brushed surfaces, and a clear domed crystal. Dials come in deep blue, black, silver, champagne or sunburst green with fine radial brushing, applied baton hour markers filled with luminous paint, a day and date window at three, and slim bright hands with a central sweep seconds. Divers have a rotating bezel with luminous pip and chunky bracelet links. Dial text is small silver capitals and a wordmark in stylised sans-serif. Mood is clean, practical, quietly sophisticated and slightly retro.'),
('Swatch', 'Europe', '1980s-90s', 'watches', 'In the style of Swatch, Swiss plastic fashion watches. Slim thin wristwatches with a round transparent or opaque moulded plastic case and a matching moulded band in one piece. Bright pop-art colours such as hot pink, neon green, cobalt blue and yellow, bold geometric patterns, polka dots, stripes and graffiti-like prints on dial and strap. Dials are simple with oversize numerals or minimalist hour lines and thin sweep seconds hands. Fine printed text, a small cross-shaped mark in a rectangle, and a flat top crystal. Mood is playful, bright, youthful and 1980s fun.'),
('Rolex', 'Europe', '1950s-present', 'watches', 'In the style of Rolex, Swiss luxury steel and gold watches. Round robust cases of polished and brushed stainless steel or yellow gold with a fluted or smooth bezel, a screw-down winding crown protected by shoulders and topped with a small crown logo, and a magnifying cyclops bubble over the date at three. Dials are glossy black, white, blue, green or champagne with applied polished hour markers and luminous dots, plus broad sword-shaped hands. Three-link Oyster-style bracelets with satin centre links and polished outer links. Lettering is crisp small serif capitals in gold or white. Mood is solid, imposing, polished and status-heavy.'),
('Omega', 'Europe', '1950s-70s', 'watches', 'In the style of Omega, Swiss sports and dress watches. Round steel cases with clean faceted lugs and a polished or brushed finish, domed hesalite-like crystals, and tachymeter bezels in black aluminium with white numerals. Dials are matte black or silver with contrasting sub-dials in chronograph models, baton hands, applied index markers with luminous infill, and a small Greek letter logo at twelve. Straps in black leather with white stitching or steel bracelets with tapering links. Lettering is crisp, slim white sans-serif. Mood is purposeful, elegant and exploratory with a vintage space-age touch.'),
('Patek Philippe', 'Europe', '1930s-present', 'watches', 'In the style of Patek Philippe, Swiss haute horlogerie. Slim round or oval cases in polished rose gold, yellow gold or platinum with elegant fine lugs, a thin bezel and a refined hand-stitched alligator leather strap in brown or black. Dials are cream, silvered or deep blue with finely guilloched surfaces, slender dauphine hands, applied gold Breguet numerals or baton markers, and subtle small seconds or moon-phase windows with small scripts. Cases have clean proportions with discreet crowns and a Calatrava-style cross mark. Typography is fine serif capitals and delicate cursive. Mood is refined, understated, heirloom and timeless.'),
('Nomos Glashutte', 'Europe', '1990s-present', 'watches', 'In the style of Nomos Glashutte, German minimalist watches. Slim round stainless steel cases with thin straight lugs, a very narrow bezel and a flat domed crystal over a pure white or silvery-white dial. The dial has slender blued steel hands, thin black Arabic numerals in a clean geometric sans-serif and a tiny subsidiary seconds dial at six, plus a thin minute track ring. Straps in plain brown or cordovan leather. Sapphire back reveals a decorated movement with stripes and blued screws. Mood is spare, precise, calm and modern.'),
('Junghans', 'Europe', '1950s-70s', 'watches', 'In the style of Junghans, German modernist clocks and watches. Round or rectangular dials with extremely clean layouts, slim baton or simple stick hands, thin black line markers or short numerals in a geometric sans-serif, and a dome-shaped crystal. Case in matte steel or gold with minimal detail. Colours are white, black, grey with occasional warm orange or yellow second hands. Table clocks are small cylinders or squares of off-white enamel or wood with tiny hole speaker-style detail. Mood is pared-back, functional and Bauhaus-like in discipline.'),
('Smeg', 'Europe', '1950s-retro', 'appliances', 'In the style of Smeg, Italian retro kitchen appliances. Curvaceous, rounded rectangular refrigerators, kettles and toasters in glossy pastel enamel colours such as cream, pastel blue, pink, mint green and red, with polished chrome handles, trim and rounded corners. Large thick metal rounded door edges recall 1950s American cars, with a bold chrome oval logo on the front. Controls are chunky chrome knobs and rounded toggles. Surfaces are shiny and seamless with a soft sheen. Mood is cheerful, nostalgic and kitchen-boutique fashionable.'),
('KitchenAid', 'North America', '1930s-present', 'appliances', 'In the style of KitchenAid, American stand mixers. A heavy cast metal body with a smooth curved bulbous top, a tilting head that pivots on a rear hinge, and a tall flat-bottomed steel or glass bowl with a curved handle. Glossy enamel in empire red, onyx black, white, pistachio, pastel blue and cream, with a polished chrome speed lever on the side and a round attachment hub at the front. Beaters and dough hooks in brushed silver. Stainless script lettering on the front. Mood is sturdy, generous and homey with a vintage curve.'),
('Dyson', 'Europe', '1990s-present', 'appliances', 'In the style of Dyson, British high-tech household machines. Transparent cyclone chambers in clear plastic reveal the inner mechanics, set against bright coloured plastic parts in purple, fuchsia, yellow, nickel grey and iron. Parts are tubular and ribbed, with exposed engineering, smooth curved plastic moulding, visible fixings and large chunky wheels. Bladeless fans are thin glossy rings on a tall tapering stand. Small colour-coded buttons and tiny LCD readouts. Lettering is small and bold. Mood is engineered, futuristic, glossy and rather industrial.'),
('Bosch Professional', 'Europe', '1990s-present', 'tools', 'In the style of Bosch Professional, German power tools. Hard bodies in a distinctive deep blue plastic with black rubberised soft grips and bold red logo marks. Compact drills and saws have ergonomic curved handles, textured grips with diamond patterns, and bright silver metal chucks. Labels are crisp white capital sans-serif text and small red warning stickers. Battery packs are blue and black with a small LED level gauge. Cases are tough blue-grey moulded boxes with silver latches. Mood is robust, ergonomic, cool and professional.'),
('Makita', 'East Asia', '1990s-present', 'tools', 'In the style of Makita, Japanese power tools. Strong teal-blue-green plastic housings with black rubberised handles and black battery packs, a red stripe on the label, and tough silver or steel metalwork. Shapes are compact and rounded with chunky triggers, ribbed overmoulded grips, and neat rows of small ventilation slots. Text is bold white capital lettering and a boxed brand mark. LED work lights and bright yellow warning labels. Mood is solid, workmanlike and cool teal.'),
('DeWalt', 'North America', '1990s-present', 'tools', 'In the style of DeWalt, American contractor power tools. Bright yellow plastic housings with black rubberised grips and black accent bands, boxy chunky shapes with strong ribbing and protective rubber bumpers. Battery packs are chunky yellow and black blocks with a small fuel gauge. Text is bold black block capitals on yellow, with heavy outlined logo panels, and small silver steel chucks. Cases are rugged yellow and black stackable boxes with big latches. Mood is loud, rugged, jobsite-ready and high-visibility.'),
('Milwaukee Tool', 'North America', '2000s-present', 'tools', 'In the style of Milwaukee Tool, American heavy-duty power tools. Signature bright red plastic housings with black rubberised grips and black battery packs, bold stripes of red against black, tough angular shapes with big chunky triggers and reinforced rubber guards. Lettering is large white or black block capitals in a heavy italic sans-serif. Metal parts are raw silver steel, with red-and-black latch cases. Mood is aggressive, rugged, masculine and industrial.'),
('Fender', 'North America', '1950s-60s', 'instruments', 'In the style of Fender, American electric guitars and amplifiers of the 1950s and 1960s. Offset double-cutaway or single-cutaway slab bodies with sleek contours, sunburst finishes fading from yellow to red to black, or solid Surf Green, Daphne Blue, Fiesta Red and cream. White or tortoiseshell pickguards, chrome knobs and bridge plates, maple necks with black dot markers, and a bold curved script logo on the headstock. Amplifiers have tweed or black vinyl cabinets, silver grille cloth, chrome corner trim and a row of cream or black knobs. Mood is bright, twangy, sunny California.'),
('Gibson', 'North America', '1950s-60s', 'instruments', 'In the style of Gibson, American electric and acoustic guitars. Carved arched-top bodies with a rich, glossy cherry red or golden sunburst finish, cream binding around the edges, and a flamed maple top. Bold mother-of-pearl block or trapezoid inlays on a dark rosewood fingerboard, gold-plated hardware, twin chrome-covered humbucking pickups, four gold barrel knobs, and a swept-back headstock with a pearl inlay logo and crown shape. Mood is rich, warm, heavy and luxurious.'),
('Marshall Amplification', 'Europe', '1960s-70s', 'instruments', 'In the style of Marshall Amplification, British guitar amplifiers. Large black vinyl-covered cabinets with a woven basket-weave cloth grille in tan or black, trimmed with gold or silver piping and a bold script logo in white on a gold or black plastic panel at the top. Control panel with a row of chunky black skirted knobs with white numerals, a pilot light in a red jewel, and a rocker switch. Stacks of tall rectangular speaker cabinets set in a wall on stage. Mood is loud, stacked, rock and roll and imposing.'),
('Moog Music', 'North America', '1970s', 'instruments', 'In the style of Moog Music, analogue synthesizers. Solid wood cabinets in dark walnut or black with a slanted control panel in black or silver, packed with chunky round knobs with white pointers, patch cords and jacks, small rocker switches, and printed white labels in a clear sans-serif. A long keyboard with white and black keys and a pitch ribbon. Colour accents are red, orange and white lines grouping the sections. Mood is warm, vintage, scientific and handcrafted.'),
('Roland', 'East Asia', '1980s', 'instruments', 'In the style of Roland, 1980s Japanese electronic instruments. Dark grey or black angular metal and plastic cases with wide control surfaces, rows of tiny coloured plastic buttons in orange, red, blue and cream, slim sliders and small red LED displays. Drum machines have rows of small rounded square pads in red, orange, yellow and white. Printed labels use fine white lettering with grouped panel lines. Synthesizers have long keyboards, wedge-like profiles and a bold stripe with the model name. Mood is techy, club-ready and boxy.'),
('Yamaha Synthesizers', 'East Asia', '1980s', 'instruments', 'In the style of Yamaha Synthesizers, 1980s digital keyboards. Long slim cream-white or black plastic bodies with flat membrane buttons in grey and a small blue-green backlit LCD display screen, slim data-entry sliders, and a full-length velocity keyboard. Silver lettering and a minimal printed grid of function labels, rounded edge corners and a three-tuning-fork logo. Mood is sleek, digital and early-electronic with soft grey and teal tones.'),
('Teenage Engineering', 'Europe', '2010s-present', 'instruments', 'In the style of Teenage Engineering, Swedish electronic music gear. Flat, thin, rectangular aluminium or white plastic slabs with exact grids of small coloured rubber buttons in orange, grey and white, tiny round knobs and bright pixel displays. Orange and neon accents, silkscreened white and black technical lettering in a small monospaced sans-serif, minimal diagrams and fine line graphics. Rounded sleeves and playful pastel-coloured carry cases. Mood is clean, geeky, graphic and playful.'),
('Nothing', 'Europe', '2020s-present', 'electronics', 'In the style of Nothing, transparent tech gadgets. Clear see-through plastic and glass casings that reveal internal components, circuit boards, screws and coils. Palette is white, black and transparent with a signature bright red dot accent. Phone backs have glowing white LED light strips arranged in segments around the camera. Typography is dot-matrix lettering with round dots forming monochrome numerals, and icons are pixelated. Edges are flat and squared with soft corners. Mood is stripped-back, nerdy, futuristic and quirky.'),
('Samsung', 'East Asia', '2010s-present', 'electronics', 'In the style of Samsung, Korean consumer electronics. Thin glossy glass slabs with curved edges, metallic frames in black, silver, gold and blue, vivid AMOLED screens with saturated colours and nearly invisible bezels. Camera modules stand out in separate circular lenses on a vertical or horizontal strip. Televisions and appliances use thin brushed metal and glossy black or white panels with minimal touch controls. Interface graphics use rounded square icons, smooth sans-serif type and soft pastel colour gradients. Mood is polished, bright, flat-glass and modern.'),
('Xiaomi', 'East Asia', '2010s-present', 'electronics', 'In the style of Xiaomi, Chinese consumer electronics. Simple matte white plastic or glass shapes with softly rounded corners, orange squared-rounded logo block, and small flat circular lens bumps. Clean minimalist products such as air purifiers, scooters and rice cookers in white and light grey with a single glowing coloured LED ring. Interface uses flat colourful icons with soft rounded corners and a friendly sans-serif font. Packaging is plain brown cardboard with a single orange square mark. Mood is clean, affordable-minimal and friendly.'),
('Bose', 'North America', '1980s-2000s', 'electronics', 'In the style of Bose, American audio products. Compact, small rounded boxes and cubes in matte black or white with fabric-covered speaker grilles, curved or tapering enclosures, and small clean lettering. Headphones have plush rounded ear cups in soft black or silver with a thin padded headband and subtle buttons. Wave radios have a smooth rounded body with a brushed silver face and tiny buttons. Surfaces are soft matte and neutral with few visible fixings. Mood is understated, comfortable and home-friendly.'),
('Sonos', 'North America', '2010s-present', 'electronics', 'In the style of Sonos, wireless speakers. Smooth matte cuboid or cylinder shapes in black or white with a perforated metal mesh grille wrapped around the whole body, and a flat top with a touch-sensitive strip of tiny glowing icons. Soft rounded corners, no visible screws, a small status LED, and a tiny mark. Soundbars are long thin horizontal slabs. Mood is quiet, domestic, matte and minimal.'),
('Zenith Radio', 'North America', '1930s-50s', 'electronics', 'In the style of Zenith Radio, American radios and televisions of the 1930s to 1950s. Wood cabinets with streamlined curved corners and a large round dial with an illuminated glass face in cream with black numerals. Bakelite knobs in black or ivory, tall slim fabric grilles with gold lines, chrome trim bars and rounded speaker panels. Early televisions have wood cabinets with a small curved glass screen and rounded edges. A lightning bolt Z logo appears at the front. Mood is polished, elegant and mid-century domestic.'),
('Philips', 'Europe', '1930s-60s', 'electronics', 'In the style of Philips, Dutch radios and appliances of the 1930s to 1960s. Wooden or bakelite cabinets with rounded edges, big round dials in glass with illuminated station names, and pale ivory or chocolate-brown plastics. Controls are big ribbed knobs and piano-style keys. Fabric grilles with vertical gold slats, and a small star and wave logo. Later products use bright plastic in cream, mustard and pastel with gently curved forms. Mood is homely, rounded and optimistic.'),
('Telefunken', 'Europe', '1950s-60s', 'electronics', 'In the style of Telefunken, German tube radios and televisions of the 1950s and 1960s. Warm polished walnut or beech cabinets with rounded fronts, large illuminated station scales in glass with green and orange glowing eyes, and slim ivory keys across the bottom edge. Gold fabric speaker grilles with ornamental slots, chrome-plated dial trim, and big cream knobs. A diamond-shaped logo sits at the front. Mood is warm, glowing, heavy and domestic.'),
('Grundig', 'Europe', '1950s-60s', 'electronics', 'In the style of Grundig, German radios and tape recorders of the 1950s and 1960s. Wood-veneer cabinets, brushed gold or chrome piano keys, large round glass scales with illuminated tuning markers and a magic-eye indicator, and pale cream or brown plastic knobs. Reel-to-reel recorders have grey-green hammerite finishes, small VU meters and neat rows of lettered buttons. A diamond-shaped mark sits on the front. Mood is solid, warm and middle-class.'),
('Kodak', 'North America', '1900s-80s', 'cameras', 'In the style of Kodak, American popular cameras and film packaging. Early cameras are leather-covered boxes with a round lens and a simple viewfinder. Mid-century models have art deco ribs and chrome stripes, then moulded plastic in the 1970s and 1980s. Packaging uses a bold yellow, red and black colour scheme with big sans-serif lettering and a red stylised K mark. Bright yellow film boxes with red panels. Mood is cheerful, familiar and snapshot-friendly.'),
('GoPro', 'North America', '2010s-present', 'cameras', 'In the style of GoPro, tough action cameras. Small matte black or dark grey rubberised cubes with a large round glass lens on the front, a tiny front screen, and a few chunky buttons with white icons on top. Mounts are bright black plastic frames with chunky tabs, three-prong folding connectors, orange-yellow or blue rubber straps and thumbscrews. Cases are transparent waterproof boxes. Typography is bold white sans-serif in a rounded style. Mood is rugged, active and outdoorsy.'),
('Nokia', 'Europe', '1990s-2000s', 'electronics', 'In the style of Nokia, Finnish mobile phones of the 1990s and 2000s. Chunky candy-bar handsets in blue-grey, black, silver or bright interchangeable coloured plastic covers, with a small monochrome green-backlit LCD showing pixel text, a rounded numeric keypad of soft rubber keys, and a prominent curved navigation key in the middle. Short stubby antennas or smooth rounded cases with a tiny speaker slot. Menu icons are simple pixel images with a friendly rounded font. Mood is tough, friendly and tactile.'),
('Ericsson', 'Europe', '1990s', 'electronics', 'In the style of Ericsson, Swedish mobile phones of the late 1990s. Slim grey or black handsets with a flip cover, a stubby retractable antenna, a small greyish-green LCD, and neat grids of rounded rectangular keys. Cool silver-blue finish, rounded corners and a clean oval logo. Telephone sets in the 1950s had a one-piece curved bakelite body in ivory, black or red, with a rotary dial and a single cord. Mood is sleek, grey and corporate.'),
('Motorola', 'North America', '1980s-2000s', 'electronics', 'In the style of Motorola, American mobile phones and radios. The 1980s brick has a huge cream-grey case with a long rubbery antenna, a chunky rectangular keypad with large grey keys, a bright red-orange LED display and a heavy black handle. The 2000s razor-thin flip phone has a brushed aluminium finish with an ultra-thin body, a flat keypad etched from a single metal sheet, and a blue backlight glow. A stylised M bat-wing mark at the top. Mood is bold, tech-era and metallic.'),
('Lenovo ThinkPad', 'East Asia', '1990s-present', 'computers', 'In the style of Lenovo ThinkPad, black business laptops. Matte black soft-touch cases with square corners and a flat slab shape, a red rubber nub in the middle of a black keyboard, scooped matte black keys with white letters and a red-dot accent on the lid near the logo. A row of red-trimmed buttons below the space bar, minimal silver trim, and flat hinges with small status LEDs. Italic white text spells the model name on the lid. Mood is serious, utilitarian and corporate.'),
('Anglepoise', 'Europe', '1930s-present', 'lighting', 'In the style of Anglepoise, British balanced-arm desk lamps. A heavy round stepped base, two long slim parallel steel arms joined by four coiled tension springs, and a conical metal shade with a rounded top. Finishes are glossy enamel in black, cream, red, pea green and grey, or polished and brushed copper and brass. The sleek lamp has an adjustable arm to any angle, a black cloth cable and a small switch on the shade. Mood is industrial, classic, hardworking and beautiful.'),
('Vitsoe', 'Europe', '1960s-present', 'furniture', 'In the style of Vitsoe, modular shelving systems. Thin vertical aluminium tracks screwed to the wall with slim aluminium shelves hung from them on small pegs. Shelves are powder-coated in white, black or light grey, or made of smooth plywood in pale birch, with sleek clean edges. Wardrobe units are made of crisp panels in matte pale colours, with narrow slots and small detailing. Everything is clean, orderly and rectilinear with thin lines and no decoration. Mood is calm, minimalist and timeless.'),
]
